---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="HabitTrack Privacy Policy: 100% private, client-side only habit tracker. Zero accounts, zero remote servers, no analytics, and zero tracking."
>
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <!-- Hero Card -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-[#1a0b2e] rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-purple-800/50 p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-sm">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/60 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-100 dark:border-emerald-800/60 mb-4">
        <span>🛡️</span>
        <span>Zero Data Collection Guarantee</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-50 tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300/80">
        Effective date: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary Box -->
    <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 border border-emerald-500/30 dark:border-emerald-700/50">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 mb-1">In Plain English:</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300/90 leading-relaxed">
        HabitTrack does not collect, record, transmit, sell, or analyze any of your data. There are no user accounts, no analytics SDKs, no tracking pixels, and no remote databases. All information you enter resides 100% locally in your browser storage.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Policy Details Card -->
    <div class="bg-white dark:bg-[#1a0b2e] rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-purple-800/50 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-8">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">1. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/85 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
          HabitTrack is engineered as an offline-first client application. We have zero visibility into your data:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-300/90">
          <li><strong>No Personal Identifiers:</strong> We do not ask for or store names, emails, phone numbers, or passwords.</li>
          <li><strong>No Habit Content:</strong> Your habit titles, positions, and completion logs never leave your physical device.</li>
          <li><strong>No Telemetry:</strong> We do not track page views, button clicks, time spent in app, or device hardware identifiers.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-purple-900/40">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">2. Local Storage Technologies</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/85 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
          The application saves your preferences and logs locally using modern browser APIs:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-3">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-[#201038] border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-purple-800/40">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100 mb-1">IndexedDB</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300/80">
              Stores habit rows and day-by-day completion logs on your physical device.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 dark:bg-[#201038] border border-slate-200/60 dark:border-purple-800/40">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100 mb-1">localStorage</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300/80">
              Stores your aesthetic preference (light mode or dark purple mode).
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-purple-900/40">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">3. Cookies & Trackers</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/85 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
          HabitTrack uses <strong>zero cookies</strong> and includes zero tracking libraries. You will never see cookie consent banners because we do not use tracking or advertising cookies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-purple-900/40">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">4. Data Deletion & Ownership</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/85 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
          You have absolute sovereignty over your habit data. You can erase any individual habit from the three-dot menu, or wipe all stored application data by clearing your browser's site data or cache at any time.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
